{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Base"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Base"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols18DirectedHypergraphP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DirectedHypergraph"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Positions "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< P_s"},{"type":"text","text":" are the source incidences, hyperedge by hyperedge in index order and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"within one in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sourceIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"P_s + q"},{"type":"text","text":" is target incidence "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"type":"text","text":", in the same order. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-incidence array is indexed by edge position. A view is a snapshot, so its own positions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only until its next mutation: the view of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", inserting"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one cell shifts every later incidence by one)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every index member reads the base’s rows, shifted where they hold hyperedges:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successorIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"text":" plus n, and of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"text":" it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"targetIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"predecessorIndices"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inHyperedgeIndices"},{"text":" plus n, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sourceIndices"},{"text":". Graph algorithms therefore run on the view without hashing a vertex. The view","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"does not offer ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_withSuccessorIndexRows"},{"text":", whose contract needs edge positions in row order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Costs are as for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceGraphView"},{"type":"text","text":": O(1) reads on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":", which stores its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incidences; on another base a hyperedge’s incidence numbers are a range, O(1), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binary-searches and selects by rank, O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on "},{"type":"codeVoic